# Nothing in this repository should ever be uploaded to Vercel from the root.
#
# The intended deployment has web/ as the Root Directory, in which case Vercel
# reads web/.vercelignore and never looks at this file. This exists for the
# case that goes wrong: a `vercel deploy` run from the repository root, where
# without it the CLI would upload the whole working tree — including 225 MB of
# live Chrome profile with real cookies and login data, and screenshots of
# whatever was on screen at the time.
#
# .gitignore does not help here. It governs Git, not the Vercel uploader.
#
# Deny everything, then allow back only the public web interface. An allowlist
# fails safe: a new folder of local state added next year is excluded because
# nobody remembered to exclude it.
*
!web/
!web/**

# Belt and braces — these stay excluded even if the allowlist above is ever
# loosened, because they are the ones that actually matter.

# Runtime state: databases, event logs, edit backups, personal profile
data/
data/browser-profile/
data/captures/
data/edits/

# The desktop agent itself. It runs on the user's PC and has no business on a
# static host: Ollama, MCP subprocesses, voice, vision and desktop control all
# require the local machine.
jarvish/
tests/
plugins/
new.py
requirements.txt
mcp.json

# Secrets and credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
credentials.json

# Local databases and logs
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log
logs/

# Models and caches
models/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.onnx
.cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Backups and scratch
*.bak
*.tmp
*.temp

# Version control and tooling
.git/
.github/
.vercel/
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
